archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0900079Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0907595Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0985307Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0993683Z ^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0993962Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0994295Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0994413Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0994514Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0995506Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0995645Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0995732Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0995930Z    if you are ready to continue.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0996037Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0996215Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0996468Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0996673Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0996845Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0996925Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0997011Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0997137Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0997228Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0997408Z    can use Nix.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0997473Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0997520Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0997603Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0997812Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.0998038Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1003019Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1003088Z I will:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1003173Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1003299Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1003534Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1003736Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1003925Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1004062Z  - install Nix in /nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1004192Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1004382Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1004562Z    /root
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1018382Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1018998Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1027622Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1027964Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1028352Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1029499Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1029698Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1044558Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1044956Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1052935Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1053316Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1053619Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1053765Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1053903Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1054074Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1054216Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1054545Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1054702Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1054773Z If you would like to
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1054962Z see the output, try like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1055440Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1055566Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1055836Z   $ sh ./install-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1055956Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1055960Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1056136Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1062943Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1063245Z been installed on this system.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1101290Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:12.1101772Z ^[[34m---- Nix config report ---------------------------------------------------------
