fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5309390Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5319636Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5421947Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5432104Z ^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5432846Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5433993Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5434393Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5434711Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5435978Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5436483Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5436802Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5437481Z    if you are ready to continue.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5437795Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5438418Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5439435Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5440503Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5441177Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5441500Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5441807Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5442447Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5442808Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5443759Z    can use Nix.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5444018Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5444218Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5444549Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5445118Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5446013Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5448848Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5449470Z I will:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5449967Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5450311Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5451016Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5451571Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5452013Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5452309Z  - install Nix in /nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5452589Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5453021Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5453704Z    /root
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5465728Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5466602Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5477592Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5478277Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5478778Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5479929Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5480605Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5498525Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5509514Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5511031Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5512026Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5512876Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5513476Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5513964Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5514421Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5514782Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5515588Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5515982Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5516103Z If you would like to
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5516410Z see the output, try like this:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5516663Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5516889Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5517397Z   $ sh ./install-nix
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5517601Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5517609Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T17:37:11.5517885Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
